## 11. Financial Definitions

### Approved annual budget

The total spending authority approved for a department or company during the financial year.

### Project allocation

The portion of a department’s approved budget reserved for a specific project.

### Commitment

An approved financial obligation that has not yet been paid or recognized as actual spending.

### Actual expense

An amount that has been paid or recorded as realized spending.

### Payment confirmation

A Finance-recorded confirmation that an approved expense was paid outside the application. Payment confirmation moves the amount from an unpaid commitment to actual spending and requires transfer-proof details for bank transfers.

### Available budget

The amount still available for new commitments.

For the prototype:

```text
Available Budget
= Allocation
− Actual Expense
− Committed but Unpaid Amount
```

### Unallocated budget

The portion of a departmental budget that has not been reserved for projects or other predefined uses.

