## 13. Request Statuses

The prototype will use the following statuses:

* Draft
* Awaiting Manager Approval
* Awaiting Finance Review
* Revision Required
* Approved — Awaiting Payment
* Payment Processing (optional)
* Rejected
* Paid

Status meanings:

| Status | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Awaiting Manager Approval | Business approval is pending. |
| Awaiting Finance Review | Finance validation and final approval are pending. |
| Approved — Awaiting Payment | All approvals are complete and the amount is an unpaid commitment. |
| Payment Processing | Finance has started external payment processing; optional for the prototype. |
| Paid | Finance confirmed payment and recorded actual spending. |
| Rejected | The request will not proceed. |
| Revision Required | The requester must edit and resubmit the request. |

For the one-day prototype, the primary workflow is:

```text
Draft
→ Awaiting Manager Approval
→ Awaiting Finance Review
→ Approved — Awaiting Payment
→ Paid
```

Alternative paths:

```text
Awaiting Manager Approval
→ Revision Required
→ Awaiting Manager Approval
```

```text
Awaiting Manager Approval
→ Rejected
```

```text
Awaiting Finance Review
→ Rejected
```

If payment processing is shown as a separate state, the final path is:

```text
Approved — Awaiting Payment
→ Payment Processing
→ Paid
```

