## 23. Prototype Acceptance Criteria

### Annual budget overview

* The user can see the FY2027 approved budget.
* Department budgets display approved, allocated, committed, actual, and available amounts.
* Clicking a department opens its detail page.

### Department detail

* The user can see department budget lines.
* The user can see all projects receiving allocations from the department.
* Department totals reconcile with the displayed allocations and spending.

### Project detail

* The Ramadan Campaign displays allocations from at least four departments.
* The total project budget equals the sum of all departmental allocations.
* The user can view committed, actual, and available amounts by department.
* The project view distinguishes paid expenses from approved but unpaid commitments.

### Expense request

* The user can create a request against a project allocation.
* The form displays the budget impact before submission.
* The system blocks requests exceeding the available amount.
* A valid request can be submitted successfully.

### Approval

* A manager can approve a submitted request.
* Finance can complete the approval.
* A fully approved request becomes `Approved — Awaiting Payment` and increases the commitment amount.
* Updated values appear on the project and department pages.
* The approval action appears in the activity history.

### Payment confirmation

* Finance can view fully approved requests awaiting payment.
* Finance can open a request and select `Record Payment`.
* The system requires payment details and mock transfer proof.
* The system blocks duplicate payment, zero or negative amounts, and amounts that differ from the approved amount.
* The request becomes `Paid` after confirmation.
* The commitment decreases and actual spending increases by the same amount.
* Available budget is not reduced twice.
* Payment details, processor, timestamp, and transfer-proof filename appear in the activity history.
* Updated values appear consistently in project, department, and annual-budget views.

### Role switching

* Users can switch between at least Requester, Manager, Finance, and Executive roles.
* Visible actions change according to the selected role.

