## 27. Key Risks

### Risk: Scope becomes too close to an ERP

Mitigation:

Keep the prototype focused on visibility, allocation, expense requests, and approval.

### Risk: Payment confirmation is confused with payment execution

Mitigation:

Label the feature as payment confirmation, keep bank execution outside the application, and use transfer proof only as mock evidence.

### Risk: Budget and cash are confused

Mitigation:

Use budget terminology consistently and exclude bank balances or treasury functions.

### Risk: Project allocations are double counted

Mitigation:

Treat allocations as reservations under department budgets, not additional company budget.

### Risk: Cross-functional ownership becomes unclear

Mitigation:

Require every allocation and request to have a department owner and budget line.

### Risk: Prototype contains many screens but no complete workflow

Mitigation:

Prioritize one end-to-end flow from annual budget to project request, approval, and payment confirmation.

